(7483098, 1190186, 172697, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Lydia:</b></div><hr/><i> I always look at an image for the challenge topic, of course, but also how I like it outside of the challenge topic.<br/> <br/>This wins on the former (It fits the topic perfectly), but it doesn''t work at all for me as a photograph outside of the challenge.<br/> <br/>I didn''t vote on this, but I''d have given it my lowest score, due to it not being a wonderful photograph on its own standing.<br/> <br/>However, I''m only one person... *grin*  And I''m only telling this to help you understand other people''s ideas, not to criticize. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>And I thank you for your feedback, Lydia!<br/> <br/>This particular one was shot with the sole purpose of entering this challenge, It''s not a picture I''m fond of, and I''m aware of the fact that it has only one leg to stand on!<br/> <br/>Maybe this is an error I make, sometimes I tend to give too much importance to the challenge fitting, rather than the absolute value of a photography.<br/> <br/>Anyway these are all different yet valid points of view.<br/> <br/>Thanks again for stopping by!</td>', 'Originally posted by Lydia: I always look at an image for the challenge topic, of course, but also how I like it outside of the challenge topic. This wins on the former (It fits the topic perfectly), but it doesn''t work at all for me as a photograph outside of the challenge. I didn''t vote on this, but I''d have given it my lowest score, due to it not being a wonderful photograph on its own standing. However, I''m only one person... *grin*  And I''m only telling this to help you understand other people''s ideas, not to criticize.   And I thank you for your feedback, Lydia! This particular one was shot with the sole purpose of entering this challenge, It''s not a picture I''m fond of, and I''m aware of the fact that it has only one leg to stand on! Maybe this is an error I make, sometimes I tend to give too much importance to the challenge fitting, rather than the absolute value of a photography. Anyway these are all different yet valid points of view. Thanks again for stopping by!', '2016-11-18 02:47:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(7483112, 1190362, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>Your single shot worked out well you have a good level of detail throughout, to be honest, I dont really see sufficient range of contrasts that bracketing would have proved beneficial. Your composition is good with the most important elements, the handles, off-centre in an appealing sort of way. Whilst there is no real impact there is a generally appealing feel to the image with the interesting detail of the ornately decorated wood and its appealing shapes. Sorry you didnt receive any comments during the challenge, hope this makes up for it.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge Your single shot worked out well you have a good level of detail throughout, to be honest, I dont really see sufficient range of contrasts that bracketing would have proved beneficial. Your composition is good with the most important elements, the handles, off-centre in an appealing sort of way. Whilst there is no real impact there is a generally appealing feel to the image with the interesting detail of the ornately decorated wood and its appealing shapes. Sorry you didnt receive any comments during the challenge, hope this makes up for it.', '2016-11-18 05:45:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(7483113, 1190129, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>Well done Janine, I think you have managed to fulfil all the elements of the challenge brief here! What a beautifully ornate doorway, thank you for your helpful and informative comments. The doorway itself, actually looks rather intimidating, like an alien about to consume you as you enter. The lighting is quite sympathetic with good detail throughout, although the door itself is a little vignetted it helps emphasise the middle doorway itself. I find the three items, 2 yellow and black and white oval in the lower right, whatever they are, rather distracting and feel they would be better cloned out.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge Well done Janine, I think you have managed to fulfil all the elements of the challenge brief here! What a beautifully ornate doorway, thank you for your helpful and informative comments. The doorway itself, actually looks rather intimidating, like an alien about to consume you as you enter. The lighting is quite sympathetic with good detail throughout, although the door itself is a little vignetted it helps emphasise the middle doorway itself. I find the three items, 2 yellow and black and white oval in the lower right, whatever they are, rather distracting and feel they would be better cloned out.', '2016-11-18 05:56:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(7483115, 1190365, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>What an unusual window! Your viewpoint with the illuminated window behind has highlighted the detail of the bells making them even more prominent and appealing, sorry couldnt resist that. You were right to consider this for mono and a good job youve done of it too, there is a good range on tones with plenty of detail throughout. Well spotted Eugene, hope you enjoyed your time in Budapest.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge What an unusual window! Your viewpoint with the illuminated window behind has highlighted the detail of the bells making them even more prominent and appealing, sorry couldnt resist that. You were right to consider this for mono and a good job youve done of it too, there is a good range on tones with plenty of detail throughout. Well spotted Eugene, hope you enjoyed your time in Budapest.', '2016-11-18 06:21:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(7483116, 1190001, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that vaguely meets the challenge<br/> <br/>Whilst your image is visually appealing with the horses as the focal point the strong backlighting dominates the shot to its detriment. There is a loss of detail in the animals but given the theme of the challenge gates would be the only obvious element to meet the challenge but your composition and lighting makes this difficult to discern. The fences are somewhat confusing in themselves it feels as though there is probably a gate on the right edge of the frame but it is not obviously apparent. Sorry you didnt receive any comments during the challenge Ken, I hope this makes up for it.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that vaguely meets the challenge Whilst your image is visually appealing with the horses as the focal point the strong backlighting dominates the shot to its detriment. There is a loss of detail in the animals but given the theme of the challenge gates would be the only obvious element to meet the challenge but your composition and lighting makes this difficult to discern. The fences are somewhat confusing in themselves it feels as though there is probably a gate on the right edge of the frame but it is not obviously apparent. Sorry you didnt receive any comments during the challenge Ken, I hope this makes up for it.', '2016-11-18 06:30:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(7483117, 1190249, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that fully meets the challenge<br/> <br/>An excellent image Marcel! I like your composition, DOF, focus viewpoint and most importantly the timing to show the suns warming effect on the cold metal as it transforms these surfaces into something very appealing and detailed. A lovely additional element is the inverted scene in the drops. You have good exposure and details throughout the image having avoided blowing the background highlights. The suns rays through the tree are another very appealing element. I have assumed the soft focus background is purely through choice of aperture and not post-processing gaussian blur? I only ask because the immediate foreground looks equally uniform in its softness. Anyway, this is a very strong image Marcel that shows good creative vision and technical handling, a very positive progression, very well done.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that fully meets the challenge An excellent image Marcel! I like your composition, DOF, focus viewpoint and most importantly the timing to show the suns warming effect on the cold metal as it transforms these surfaces into something very appealing and detailed. A lovely additional element is the inverted scene in the drops. You have good exposure and details throughout the image having avoided blowing the background highlights. The suns rays through the tree are another very appealing element. I have assumed the soft focus background is purely through choice of aperture and not post-processing gaussian blur? I only ask because the immediate foreground looks equally uniform in its softness. Anyway, this is a very strong image Marcel that shows good creative vision and technical handling, a very positive progression, very well done.', '2016-11-18 06:41:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(7483118, 1190343, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that fully meets the challenge<br/> <br/>A good and interesting choice for the challenge. Your composition is very appealing with the padlock nicely off-centre and leading us  nicely into the soft-focus locking aspect of the draw bolt that retains attention on the padlock in an appealing way. The texture and weather worn look of the wood adds to the overall appeal of the image as a whole. Well done Faio</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that fully meets the challenge A good and interesting choice for the challenge. Your composition is very appealing with the padlock nicely off-centre and leading us  nicely into the soft-focus locking aspect of the draw bolt that retains attention on the padlock in an appealing way. The texture and weather worn look of the wood adds to the overall appeal of the image as a whole. Well done Faio', '2016-11-18 06:47:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(7483187, 1189801, 115814, '<td valign="top">Quirky and cool. Trying to imagine the context of this installation(?) Regardless it worked to keep me looking and coming back.</td>', 'Quirky and cool. Trying to imagine the context of this installation(?) Regardless it worked to keep me looking and coming back.', '2016-11-19 00:59:08.000000', NULL, 0),
